<p>Terms as Bayan uses them; each link goes to the full treatment.</p>

<h2 id="terms">Terms</h2>
<dl>
<dt id="arena">arena</dt>
<dd>Memory for many values, freed together; see <a href="memory.html">Memory</a>.</dd>

<dt id="attribute">attribute</dt>
<dd>A marker on a declaration, written <code>@</code>, such as <code>@sealed</code>.</dd>

<dt id="because">because</dt>
<dd>The clause giving why a safety bypass is acceptable; <code>bayan audit</code> prints them all.</dd>

<dt id="bypass">bypass</dt>
<dd>Code overriding a safety rule such as <code>trustUnchecked()</code>; it always carries a <code>because</code>.</dd>

<dt id="byn-code">BYN code</dt>
<dd>A diagnostic identifier such as BYN2015; all codes are in the <a href="ref-diagnostics.html">diagnostics index</a>.</dd>

<dt id="canonical">canonical form</dt>
<dd>The one spelling the compiler accepts; others are input forms.</dd>

<dt id="catch">catch</dt>
<dd>Handles a failure at the call that produced it; see <a href="errors.html">Errors</a>.</dd>

<dt id="codec">codec</dt>
<dd>A standard-library type converting between bytes and another representation, such as <code>Utf8</code>; see <a href="ref-std.html#codecs">codecs</a>.</dd>

<dt id="distinct">distinct type</dt>
<dd>A type declared <code>type distinct</code>: another type's representation, not interchangeable with it.</dd>

<dt id="effect">effect</dt>
<dd>A capability a function needs, listed after <code>uses</code>.</dd>

<dt id="fails">fails</dt>
<dd>The signature part naming the error type a function can fail with.</dd>

<dt id="fiber">fiber</dt>
<dd>A lightweight task started with <code>async</code>; see <a href="cookbook-concurrency.html">the concurrency cookbook</a>.</dd>

<dt id="head-first">head-first</dt>
<dd>Declaration order: kind before name.</dd>

<dt id="input-form">input form</dt>
<dd>A spelling the compiler recognises and rewrites to canonical form, such as a trailing <code>;</code>; <code>bayan format</code> applies it.</dd>

<dt id="module">module</dt>
<dd>A directory of <code>.byn</code> files compiled together.</dd>

<dt id="package">package</dt>
<dd>A directory with a <code>package.byn</code> manifest; see <a href="ref-cli.html#projects">projects</a>.</dd>

<dt id="particle">particle</dt>
<dd>One of the argument labels <code>from to until through at by for as</code>.</dd>

<dt id="ref-this">ref this</dt>
<dd>Marks a method that can change its receiver.</dd>

<dt id="requires">requires</dt>
<dd>A condition on a type, checked at construction.</dd>

<dt id="result">Result</dt>
<dd>What a <code>catch</code> produces: a success or an error; some standard-library calls return one directly.</dd>

<dt id="rune">rune</dt>
<dd>One Unicode scalar value.</dd>

<dt id="span">span</dt>
<dd>A view of a run of values owned by something else; cheap, and it does not copy.</dd>

<dt id="typestate">typestate</dt>
<dd>A type whose methods depend on its state, checked at compile time.</dd>

<dt id="trusted">trusted and untrusted</dt>
<dd>Outside data is untrusted until validated.</dd>

<dt id="union-error">union error</dt>
<dd>A declared set of error cases a function can fail with.</dd>

<dt id="unit">unit</dt>
<dd>A distinct numeric type such as seconds or bytes; see <a href="ref-design.html#units">units</a>.</dd>
</dl>
